      "status": "ok",
      "output": {
        "decision": "answer",
        "reason": "The evidence includes the authors' discussion (Discussion section) offering explanations for why Twitter data performs better/differently in language-inventory predictions. Specifically, they observe Twitter matches populations better when weighted by GDP and worse when weighted by internet-usage, implying Twitter represents wealthier populations; alternatively, their Twitter collection is based on urban areas, which tend to be wealthier. They also note Twitter has fewer missing languages (lower false negatives), consistent with it making better predictions about language inventory. However, strictly the authors present these as interpretations/hypotheses about representativeness rather than a definitive hypothesis specifically framed as 'why Twitter predicts language inventory better', and they note more research is needed on false positives. The evidence supports an affirmative answer with these qualifications."
      },
      "elapsed_ms": 3020.093399914913
